BT /F2 22 Tf 72 740 Td (Introduction to Photosynthesis) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 700 Td (Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants use sunlight to make their own) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 682 Td (food. It takes place mainly in the leaves, inside tiny structures called) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 664 Td (chloroplasts. Chlorophyll is a green pigment that absorbs light energy. During) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 646 Td (photosynthesis, plants take in carbon dioxide from the air and water from the soil.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 628 Td (They release oxygen as a by-product, which is essential for most living organisms on) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 610 Td (Earth. Scientists estimate that about 70 percent of the oxygen in our atmosphere) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 592 Td (comes from marine plants and algae.) Tj ET
