BT /F2 22 Tf 72 740 Td (The Light Reactions) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 700 Td (The first stage of photosynthesis is known as the light-dependent reactions. These) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 682 Td (reactions occur in the thylakoid membranes of the chloroplast. Light energy is used) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 664 Td (to split water molecules into hydrogen and oxygen. The energy is stored temporarily) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 646 Td (in molecules called ATP and NADPH. Without sunlight, these reactions cannot happen,) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 628 Td (which is why plants grow slowly in dark places.) Tj ET
endstream
